{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 49, :comments ["<b>And there was no missing.</b> Not one was lacking. Its Targum is לָא שְׁגָא — that too is in Aramaic a term of lacking, as in ״אָנֹכִי אֲחַטֶּנָּה״ (Genesis 31), whose Targum is ״דַּהֲוַת שָׁגְיָא מִמִּנְיָנָא״, and likewise ״כִּי יִפָּקֵד מוֹשָׁבֶךָ״ (1 Samuel 20) — the place of your seat will be lacking the man accustomed to sit there, and likewise ״וַיִּפָּקֵד מְקוֹם דָּוִד״ (ibid.) — his place was lacking, with no man sitting there."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:13:31.219761893Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}